    ],
    "word_count": 103,
    "html": "<p>Roy Speer's journey towards a legal career stalled when his money ran out in Texas. The future television-shopping entrepreneur found work at the Texas School for the Deaf, then combined employment with college study. He eventually returned to Florida for law school at Stetson, where he lived on campus throughout his studies.</p>\r\n<p>Speer paid for his training by working overnight as an electronics technician while attending classes during the day. Before his shifts, the parents of fellow student Elizabeth Kovachevich regularly fed him. Their friendship continued after graduation, and he later served on Stetson's law-school board of overseers and as a university trustee.</p>\r\n"
